From 1c11c2695fe0b08992ad76119589ac22ddf839fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RCTF Agent <agent@example.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 16:34:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] RCTF: add integration test suite for own-appointment scoping
 + doctor login creation

- New tests/rctf_doctor_scoping_tests.rs covering Section 8 tests A-N:
  own-list scoping (malicious doctor_filter ignored), single-read
  not-found on cross-doctor id, update/status-change ownership +
  reassignment-block, stats scoping, unlinked-profile error, full-access
  regression, and create_login_for_doctor happy/duplicate/unauthorized/
  username-collision paths.

- Extracted update_appointment_core / update_appointment_status_core
  (AERP extraction pattern) so the RCTF ownership-scoping logic is
  testable without a live Wry AppHandle (WhatsApp notifications, which
  need the real runtime, stay in the thin #[tauri::command] wrapper).

- Fixed a real regression this branch introduced against the EXISTING
  test suite, found while building the new tests:
    * tests/ipc_posture_tests.rs: the new appointments guard helpers
      (require_appointment_read_scope / require_appointment_mutation_scope)
      weren't recognized by the STRIDE guard-token scan; added them to
      GUARD_TOKENS and registered the two update_* -> *_core delegations
      in CORE_DELEGATES.
    * tests/session_tests.rs: three UpdateUserRequest struct literals were
      missing the new phone/qualification fields (compile error).
    * src/commands/search.rs: doctors lost appointment search results
      entirely (test_sst4 asserted they'd see them) -- gave the
      appointments section of global search an own-scoped branch for
      AppointmentsViewOwn, same pattern as everywhere else.

NOTE: still unexecuted in this environment (no cargo/DB here) -- run
  cargo test --features hms-integration-tests --tests --test rctf_doctor_scoping_tests
  cargo test --features hms-integration-tests --tests --test ipc_posture_tests
  cargo test --features hms-integration-tests --tests --test session_tests
  cargo test --features hms-integration-tests --tests --test search_tests
before trusting this.
